# "If it's attached to a creature you control" (CR 603.4). Bot1 takes Bot2's Grizzly Bears with Act of Treason, then puts
# Bot2's Skullclamp on them with Stolen Uniform, and the 3/1 Bears attack Bot2. In the cleanup step both "until end of
# turn" control effects end at once (CR 514.2): as Bot1 loses control of the Skullclamp, it is attached to a creature Bot2
# controls, so the delayed ability does not trigger, and the Skullclamp stays on the Bears.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Black Lotus
Act of Treason
Stolen Uniform
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Grizzly Bears
Skullclamp
Mountain x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Skullclamp.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Grizzly Bears.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Act of Treason.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Stolen Uniform.Cast
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Skullclamp)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Skullclamp.AttachedTo = Grizzly Bears
Bot1.Attack(Grizzly Bears > Bot2)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Skullclamp.AttachedTo = Grizzly Bears

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Mox Ruby
Bot1.Graveyard = Stolen Uniform; Act of Treason; Black Lotus
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Mox Emerald; Mountain; Grizzly Bears; Skullclamp
Bot2.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.Toughness = 1
Bot2.Battlefield.Skullclamp.AttachedTo = Grizzly Bears
